  "body": "## Problem and behavior\n\nThe existing single/batch social profile handlers ignored the requesting principal and could return names, avatars, bios and cities after a canonical block or closure. This patch preserves both routes and DTOs, revalidates bearer authority, and filters whole profiles in one PostgreSQL statement snapshot. Missing and denied single profiles both return generic 404. Mute, Discover opt-out and absent connection do not become new profile-privacy rules.\n\n## Dependencies and review order\n\nDepends on draft #390 at `44a1c7bed` (which depends on #386/#382/#377). #391 is parallel chat client isolation; #394 records DM/client verification evidence. No other branch is merged. Review the 41-line additive SQL, 95-line adapter, model, HTTP tests, then generated/evidence files. Remains draft because platform-wide legacy identity surfaces and hosted qualification are incomplete.\n\n## Verification actually run\n\n- TLC safety/progress: 20,166 generated / 5,760 distinct states; all three unsafe variants fail their intended invariants.\n- 2,880 observed model outcomes pass PostgreSQL; deliberately permissive SQL fails case 51. Existing 1,440 DM cases still pass.\n- Real bearer/PostgreSQL HTTP: **104 examples, zero failures**, including 11 profile cases.\n- Final Stack build/test: **2,542 examples, zero failures**, process exit 0. Catalog audit exit 0 with pinned mobile checkout.\n- Complete-schema PostgreSQL 17 fixture: migration apply/reapply and pause preserve data and denial rules.\n- Synthetic SQL benchmark: 10,005 accounts, degrees 0/10,004, batches 1/100, 40 paired samples. Final protected p95 12.11\u201343.76ms passes the previously declared 50ms threshold. Initial scalar version failed at 76.33ms; unchanged threshold prompted bulk policy joins. Reference is an unprotected joined projection, not whole legacy-handler latency. Shared-host noise and production limits documented.\n- Hosted CI pending; no earlier PR result is counted as this branch passing.\n\n## Migration, flags and rollback\n\nApply `2026-09-15_social_v2_profile_reads.sql` after #390 prerequisites, before routing this application version against the social foundation. Additive STABLE functions only: no table rewrite, backfill, new service or production activation. Missing foundation retains old compatibility behavior; incomplete foundation returns 503. Current `SOCIAL_V2_ENABLED`/database gates remain inactive in production; activation memory/pair/closure denials survive pause.\n\nRollback pauses new features while retaining this profile adapter and authoritative denials. Do not restore old readers/drop enforcement after activation. All old instances must be drained before future activation. No post-migration user writes are deleted. Destructive cleanup is separately reviewed.\n\n## Limits and operational handoff\n\n[Policy, traceability, reproduction, failed experiments and acceptance statuses](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/blob/feat/social-profile-read-boundary-20260915/docs/social/profile-read-boundary.md). Generated model cases and actual result logs are committed. Session locking is qualified by the existing SessionBoundary model. This bounded account-only model does not prove delegation, public media retrieval, arbitrary concurrency or the whole production app. Followers/friends/suggestions/search/notifications and remaining client cache surfaces still block broad rollout. Prior provider-triggered deployment exception remains unresolved; no deployment command, merge or production flag activation was issued here.\n",
